			],
			"Message": "docs(Rest): Enhance architecture documentation with emojis and inline formatting\n\nRefine the `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` file for the `Rest` component by adding section-specific emojis to improve navigation and visual hierarchy. Apply consistent inline code formatting (backticks) to technical terms, file paths, and configuration flags throughout the document.\n\nUpdate the \"Related Documentation\" section to use full GitHub repository URLs instead of relative paths, ensuring links remain functional when viewed on GitHub. Standardize the \"Module Map\" table alignment and adjust the \"Overview\" section to clearly list key capabilities as bullet points.\n\nThese changes improve the document's readability, visual consistency, and link reliability for developers referencing the OXC compiler pipeline.",
			"SHA": "ca2c6e261ee6120951bcc21f370e4f372c0f7b68"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T22:33:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Rest): Add comprehensive architecture documentation\n\nCreate `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` to detail the design and operation of the Rest component, the high-performance TypeScript compiler built on the OXC toolchain.\n\nThe document covers the OXC compilation pipeline (Parse, Semantic Analysis, Transform, Codegen, Bundle), parallel processing via Rayon, and integration with the Output element via the `RestPlugin`. It includes visual diagrams (Mermaid and ASCII) illustrating the module map and data flow, as well as detailed CLI usage examples and performance benchmarks comparing Rest against esbuild.\n\nThis addition provides developers with a clear reference for the compiler's internal structure and its role in the Land ecosystem's build pipeline.",
			"SHA": "a0e2742b37651e9d75bb562f6a7ee80378f1cd58"
		}
